msgid "``em.extensions`` — installing and enabling extensions"
msgstr ""

msgid "Generated for em API |api| from the docstrings of :mod:`s3dgraphy.em.extensions`."
msgstr ""

msgid "``em.extensions`` — install, list, enable from disk (phase 1, the plan's §5.1)."
msgstr ""

msgid "The library that does it is :mod:`s3dgraphy.extensions` (W21, W19); this is its face in ``em``, the same in a console, a script and Blender. It never asks a question: the trust of a ``[code]`` section is an argument (``trust=True``), and :func:`preview` says beforehand what an archive is made of and whether the question is needed — a window asks, a script decides with its eyes open."
msgstr ""

msgid "Bases: :py:class:`object`"
msgstr ""

msgid "``em.extensions``."
msgstr ""

msgid "The two panels of the confirmation (data, code), nothing written."
msgstr ""

msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

msgid "Return type"
msgstr ""

msgid "Everything wrong with an archive: ``{ok, errors, warnings}``, each problem in English and Italian."
msgstr ""

msgid "Install from disk (a folder or a zip): data first, code after. A ``[code]`` section needs ``trust=True`` — said by :func:`preview`; ``parts=\"data\"`` is «Data only»."
msgstr ""

msgid "Install a newer archive over an installed extension, section by section: changed code replaces the active one, changed data installs beside the old, an unchanged section is left alone."
msgstr ""

msgid "a folder or a zip."
msgstr ""

msgid "accept a ``[code]`` section (see :meth:`preview`)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Returns"
msgstr ""

msgid "the install report."
msgstr ""

msgid "What is installed on this machine, by parts."
msgstr ""

msgid "The installed extension ``eid`` (as in :meth:`list`), or None."
msgstr ""

msgid "Make a code version the active one of its id. It is LOADED by the host at its next start (W14): Python does not unload a module well."
msgstr ""

msgid "Turn off the code of ``eid`` (from the host's next start)."
msgstr ""

msgid "False when it was not enabled."
msgstr ""

msgid "The active code versions for ``host`` (default: the current host; the command line, ``none``, sees them all)."
msgstr ""

msgid "What each kind of removal of ``eid`` would do, before doing it: the code that goes with the data, who requires the data, the vocabularies nobody else brings."
msgstr ""

msgid "``part``: ``code`` · ``data`` · ``all``. The vocabularies stay on the machine unless ``purge_vocabularies`` (D-19), the plugin's own state unless ``purge_user_data`` (X3)."
msgstr ""

msgid "The curator's folder → ``<id>-<version>.zip`` (as the command line)."
msgstr ""

msgid "W15a · the plugins' development folder as set (``None``: not set)."
msgstr ""

msgid "W15a · set (or clear, ``None``) the development folder of this machine. Its plugins load where they are, marked «development, not verified», only when the host says so (EMStudio: «Funzioni sperimentali»)."
msgstr ""

msgid "W15a · the development folder and the plugins in it, with their problems."
msgstr ""

msgid "The repositories added on this machine (never their tokens)."
msgstr ""

msgid "*Repository ▸ +*: an ``index.json`` by URL, ``file://`` or a folder (a NAS). ``trust_reviews`` (X4): its reviews count here (default: the official index's only). ``keys`` (X8): its minisign public keys — with them, index and archives signed or refused."
msgstr ""

msgid "The minisign public keys of ``repo``: read (``keys=None``) or replaced (``[]``: no longer signed). The cached index stays only if it verifies."
msgstr ""

msgid "What the installer says of the ``.minisig`` beside an archive: ``signed`` / ``unknown_key`` / ``bad``, or ``None`` (not signed)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Whether the reviews of ``repo`` count on this machine (what is installed is looked at again)."
msgstr ""

msgid "The installed codes: ``verified``, ``reviewed`` (by, on, as, repo), ``trusted_by``."
msgstr ""

msgid "Forget a repository and its cached index. What was installed from it stays installed."
msgstr ""

msgid "False when there was no such repository."
msgstr ""

msgid "Read the index again (http(s) only with ``online_access``)."
msgstr ""

msgid "What the repositories offer, with what this machine has."
msgstr ""

msgid "Install from a repository: the archive checked against the index, the missing requirements first (their code only with ``trust_requires``)."
msgstr ""

msgid "«Allow online access» (set it in the host's window, or ``s3dgraphy.extensions.set_online_access``)."
msgstr ""

msgid "«Check for updates»: the indexes read again (https only with ``online_access``), what is newer, and which update would ask the trust again."
msgstr ""

msgid "«Update all»: an update that would ask the trust question again waits in ``needs_trust`` unless its id is in ``trust``."
msgstr ""

msgid "The data and code versions of ``eid`` on this machine, side by side."
msgstr ""

msgid "An older (or newer) code version already on disk made the active one — no download; the host loads it at its next start."
msgstr ""

msgid "One version of the code (not the one in use) or of the data."
msgstr ""

msgid "What nothing in the register owns, removed (``dry_run``: said)."
msgstr ""

msgid "«This file uses stat 1.0.0, 1.1.0 is here»: for the packages the open document declares (or ``declared``), the newer version installed here, how much it changes, and for a major the CHANGELOG."
msgstr ""

msgid "The answer «yes»: the open document declares ``ref`` at ``version`` (written at the next save; the packages read again now). Returns the new ``header.profiles``."
msgstr ""
